Ire/Vivek — quick status:

- Node sample (node-integ-sample) and Python sample (py-integ-sample) created and pushed to drive: https://drive.redwood.internal/drive/folders/integify-sdk-samples (read-only link sent to Integrify).
- Included short docs: install, base_url override, retry helper (exponential jitter), and a fallback example that falls back to the REST client when SDK init fails.
- Attached a zip of snippets for Paul if they want to drop them into their repo (snippets.zip referenced in drive).

Sample retry snippet (Node) — simple pattern used in the sample:

function exponentialBackoff(attempt) {
  const base = 250;
  return Math.min(Math.pow(2, attempt) * base + Math.random() * 100, 10000);
}

// pseudo:
await sdk.call(request, { retries: 3, backoff: exponentialBackoff });

